SUMMARY:Adult Fall Program - QWERT: Type in - Type Writing Program
DESCRIPTION:Typewriter Type-In with QWERT Poetry\n\nUnplug and tap into your words! Join QWERT Poetry for a hands-on Typewriter Type-In\, open to writers and non-writers alike. Pierce of QWERT Poetry will guide participants through the mechanics of manual typewriters (no experience needed) and offer writing prompts to help you get started.\n\nSix fully functional manual typewriters will be set up with paper\, envelopes\, and wax seals\, along with character cards describing each machine and how-to sheets for reference. By the end of the session\, every participant will walk away with a finished piece of writing.\n\nNo experience necessary — just bring your curiosity!
LOCATION:Pavonia Branch
CATEGORIES:October, Popular Events > Arts and Crafts Events, Popular Events > Educational Workshops, Popular Events > Social Gatherings
UID:LibCal-17422-17391577
URL:https://jclibrary.libcal.com/event/17391577
END:VEVENT
